<title>USA: Philadelphia Fed revises 1996 manufacturing survey.</title>
<headline>Philadelphia Fed revises 1996 manufacturing survey.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve Bank of Philadelphia on Tuesday reported historical revisions to its business outlook survey.</p>
<p>The January 1997 report is scheduled for release on Thursday.</p>
<p>The following are the revisions to the December 1996 report:</p>
<p>			   Original   Revised   Change</p>
<p>General Business	 -2.2	-6.2     -4.0</p>
<p>Conditions</p>
<p>New Orders		  1.9	-2.9     -4.8</p>
<p>Shipments		   4.9	 4.1     -0.8</p>
<p>Unfilled Orders	  -9.0     -15.5     -6.5</p>
<p>Delivery Times	   -9.4     -13.4     -4.0</p>
<p>Inventories		-0.9	-6.6     -5.7</p>
<p>Prices Paid		13.9	14.4	0.5</p>
<p>Prices Received	   6.2	 3.3     -2.9</p>
<p>Number of Employees    -1.6	-3.2     -1.6</p>
<p>Avg. Employee Workweek -1.6	-4.4     -2.8</p>
<p>(( -- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-869-1660 ))</p>
</text>
